cm-over-title":"Bridging the Digital-Physical Gap","bcm-over-desc":"While existing benchmarks test pristine digital documents — we evaluate the messy real world","bcm-over-card-1":"Digital Documents vs Real-World Captures","bcm-over-card-2":"Lack of Controlled Correspondence","bcm-over-card-3":"Full-Scale Physical Reconstruction","bcm-over-card-desc-1":"Models scoring 95%+ on digital benchmarks fail catastrophically on real-world captures — curved book spines, screen photographs, and non-uniform illumination all pose fatal challenges.","bcm-over-card-desc-2":"Existing in-the-wild datasets lack one-to-one correspondence with their digital counterparts, making it impossible to precisely measure the impact of real-world interference on model performance — systematic comparative analysis remains out of reach.","bcm-over-card-desc-3":"We perform a full-scale physical reconstruction of all 1,355 pages of OmniDocBench v1.5 across five physical scenarios, preserving complete ground-truth mappings to enable rigorous factor-wise causal attribution analysis.","bcm-scenarios-title":"Five Physical Scenarios","bcm-scenarios-desc":"Each scenario isolates a distinct real-world degradation factor","bcm-scenarios-btn-1":"Scanning","bcm-scenarios-btn-2":"Warping","bcm-scenarios-btn-3":"Screen-Photography","bcm-scenarios-btn-4":"Illumination","bcm-scenarios-btn-5":"Skew","bcm-scenarios-desc-1":"Evaluates parsing performance under controlled high-resolution conditions while introducing authentic paper textures and digitization noise. Covers the full spectrum of digitization artifacts commonly found in archival and office environments.","bcm-scenarios-desc-2":"Simulates non-rigid physical deformations encountered during document handling. The diverse geometric distortions provide a rigorous test for the model's spatial robustness.","bcm-scenarios-desc-3":"Replicates the secondary capture of documents displayed on digital terminals. Ensures a systematic assessment across varying pixel structures and moiré patterns.","bcm-scenarios-desc-4":"Examines parsing resilience under non-uniform lighting conditions. Probes the model's ability to maintain semantic consistency under significant contrast perturbations.","bcm-scenarios-desc-5":"Models 3D perspective distortions inherent in handheld photography. Large-angle perspective tilting induces a \"line compression\" effect, representing one of the most challenging physical scenarios.","bcm-scenarios-sub":"Sub-conditions","bcm-meth-title":"Rigorous Physical Data Acquisition Pipeline","bcm-meth-desc":"Professional-grade printing and heterogeneous multi-device capture","bcm-meth-card-1":"High-Fidelity Printing","bcm-meth-card-2":"Physical Scene Construction","bcm-meth-card-3":"Multi-Device Capture","bcm-meth-card-4":"Quality Audit","bcm-meth-desc-1":"Canon C5840 · 1200 dpi A3/A4 size-aware printing","bcm-meth-desc-2":"5 scenarios × multiple sub-conditions = comprehensive real-world configurations","bcm-meth-desc-3":"Apple · Xiaomi · OPPO heterogeneous hardware matrix","bcm-meth-desc-4":"3-round inspection: automated anomaly detection + expert manual verification","bcm-callout-title":"GT Inheritance Strategy","bcm-callout-text":"Zero-modification reuse of OmniDocBench v1.5's JSON annotations (layout, tables, formulas, text, read order), ensuring strict evaluation comparability.","bcm-board-title":"Leaderboard","bcm-board-desc":"Model rankings evaluated across 5 real-world physical scenarios","bcm-board-text-1":"The compact specialized VLM PaddleOCR-VL-1.5 (0.9B parameters) achieves an Overall score of 92.05,","bcm-board-text-2":"consistently outperforming much larger general-purpose models such as Qwen3-VL-235B (88.90) and Gemini-3 Pro (89.24).","bcm-board-note":"In the leaderboard, Formula is evaluated using the CDM metric, Table uses the TEDS metric, and the scores for Text and ReadOrder are calculated as (1 - Edit Distance) × 100%.","bcm-ds-title":"Dataset and Resources","bcm-ds-desc":"Complete benchmark dat